---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Meet Amy — the Dallasite behind The Haps Dallas blog.">
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-14 w-full">

    <!-- Profile card -->
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <div
        class="w-24 h-24 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-white text-4xl font-extrabold mx-auto mb-4 shadow-lg"
        style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-pink-hot), var(--color-purple)); font-family: var(--font-family-display);"
      >
        A
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-1" style="font-family: var(--font-family-display); color: var(--color-purple-dark);">
        hi, i'm Amy! 👋
      </h1>
      <p class="font-extrabold text-sm" style="color: var(--color-pink-hot);">✨ lifelong Dallasite & total DFW enthusiast ✨</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl p-8 shadow-md border-2 border-pink-100 prose max-w-none" style="color: var(--color-dark);">
      <p>
        I've lived in Dallas my whole life, and I <em>still</em> get genuinely excited about discovering something new here.
        There's so much going on in this city <strong>all of the time</strong> — great restaurants opening, events happening
        every weekend, parks and trails and museums that deserve way more love than they get.
      </p>

      <p>
        I started The Haps Dallas because I kept telling friends and family about things to do and places to try,
        and eventually it just made sense to write it all down in one place. My goal is simple: help you get off
        your couch and actually experience the amazing city we live in. You're welcome. 😄
      </p>

      <h2>what you'll find here 💕</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dining picks</strong> — new spots, old favorites, hidden gems</li>
        <li><strong>Weekend activities</strong> — because "I don't know, what do you want to do?" is not an answer</li>
        <li><strong>Outdoor adventures</strong> — parks, trails, lakes, and all the DFW outdoors</li>
        <li><strong>Arts & culture</strong> — the Dallas Arts District is world-class and we should all use it more!</li>
        <li><strong>Free & cheap finds</strong> — having a great time doesn't require spending a lot of money</li>
        <li><strong>Family-friendly picks</strong> — things to do with kids that adults also actually enjoy</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>a few of my faves 🌸</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Hopdoddy's Burger Bar</strong> — my forever go-to burger spot</li>
        <li><strong>Klyde Warren Park</strong> — a perfect afternoon every single time</li>
        <li><strong>Nasher Sculpture Center</strong> — one of the most beautiful places in the city</li>
        <li><strong>Dallas Arboretum in spring</strong> — never gets old, I could go every year</li>
        <li><strong>Rangers game at Globe Life Field</strong> — world-class ballpark experience</li>
        <li><strong>Katy Trail on a Sunday morning</strong> — the classic Dallas move</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Dallas has so much to offer. Let's explore it together! 💖
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
